            "content": "# Candidate: raw-value histogram binning\n\nIssue: /code/upstream-issues/langfuse-15208.md (enterprise_452a1a7f3eb80e14cfc4d7a0)\n\nCorrectness contract: compute min, range, and bucket placement from raw numeric scores. Round only generated display labels, selecting precision from bin width so adjacent edges remain distinct. Regression: 0.857 with seven bins over [0, 1] belongs in bin index 5, while 1 remains in the final bin.\n\nChanged code: /code/langfuse/web/src/features/dashboard/lib/score-analytics-utils.ts\nRegression test: /code/langfuse/web/src/__tests__/server/score-analytics-utils.servertest.ts\n\nValidation attempted: pnpm --filter web run test score-analytics-utils.servertest.ts. The mounted source snapshot cannot start pnpm because the repository references missing inherited file patches/next-auth@4.24.15.patch (ENOENT), before Vitest runs.\n\nInternal evidence: /knowledge/company/sources/slack/eng-ml/2334567001-multilang-calibration-bin-edge-bug.json and /knowledge/company/sources/confluence/applied-ml-and-evals/eval-harness/ensemble-eval-orchestration-and-weighting-guidelines-2026.json support deterministic raw bin edges and reproducible aggregation semantics.",
